# IAX-9 — the node's first over: a full Voice frame and the mini frames that
# follow it (RFC 5456 §8.1.2).
#
# Cut from the same session as `live-call-signalling.hex` — `connect3.pcap`,
# the maintainer's own capture against their own ASL3 node, 2026-08-09; the
# provenance note there covers this file too.
#
# This is the §8.1.2 switch on the wire: one full Voice frame naming µ-law and
# carrying a 32-bit time-stamp, then a run of mini frames that carry only the
# low 16 bits and no codec at all. The receiver has to pin the format from the
# full frame and expand every time-stamp after it against that anchor.
#
# The node's mini frames arrive one per 20 ms of media, at 20 ms intervals of
# wall clock — unlike ours, which leave in bursts of five (that is IAX-10).
#
# The gaps in the indices are our own outbound datagrams, which this file does
# not carry; the node's stream itself is unbroken, 2980 ms then 3000, 3020, …
# 3220, one frame per 20 ms with nothing missing.
#
# Machine-generated. The captures themselves are not in the repository —
# they are the maintainer's own, and large. Regenerate with:
#   scripts/pcap-to-fixture.py connect3.pcap --stream 0 --dir in --range 20:43
# Capture SHA-256: c9a1cbd6a973a94720086b3f22d6d996544693056db5c827f07533b873e6000d
#
# Each datagram is the UDP payload verbatim — the octets RFC 5456 §5
# defines as an IAX2 frame. `[n]` is the datagram's index in the capture
# stream, so a gap in the indices is a datagram deliberately left out.

# [20] 2.962s <== full  15069->1     ts       2980 O  4 I  4  VOICE fmt 4  160B
badd 0001 00000ba4 04 04 02 04 
# [22] 2.983s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3000  160B audio
3add 0bb8 
# [23] 3.004s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3020  160B audio
3add 0bcc 
# [29] 3.023s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3040  160B audio
3add 0be0 
# [30] 3.042s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3060  160B audio
3add 0bf4 
# [31] 3.063s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3080  160B audio
3add 0c08 
# [32] 3.084s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3100  160B audio
3add 0c1c 
# [33] 3.103s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3120  160B audio
3add 0c30 
# [39] 3.123s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3140  160B audio
3add 0c44 
# [40] 3.142s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3160  160B audio
3add 0c58 
# [41] 3.163s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3180  160B audio
3add 0c6c 
# [42] 3.183s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3200  160B audio
3add 0c80 
# [43] 3.202s <== mini  call 15069  ts  3220  160B audio
3add 0c94 
